1
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:05,850
So, this pattern here is the Tangga Beji [Beji's Ladder] pattern

2
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:09,970
So for this pua pattern, with a size this big, its fold/layer (tipan),

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:14,430
because of that, when we perform mangkal

4
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:25,890
So here, giving it this shape - this is the bamboo shoot tip (pucuk rebung).

5
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:31,610
And this corner, these are the crawling centipede feet (kaki kemebai bejalai).

6
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:37,520
So here, this is the base of the tree

7
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:42,360
This is Beji, who is going to climb this tree.

8
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:46,820
The reason Beji wanted to climb to the heavens [was to reach the gods],

9
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:53,300
but this tree, it was an Entepung tree that Beji used back then.

10
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:58,380
The reason he wanted to climb to the heavens was to follow his brother, Sumping,

11
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:03,170
because Sumping had gone up to the heavens before Beji.

12
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:07,290
But Sumping could no longer be reached,

13
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:10,920
because he jumped right off the edge of the sky (nyumping tisi langit).

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,500
We actually have a pua pattern of Sumping at our longhouse over there.

15
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:20,060
Just a little more and it would have reached the heavens,

16
00:01:22,150 --> 00:01:26,870
But then the entepung pillar broke.

17
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:31,250
It had rotted away

18
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:37,420
Then it collapsed, and fell all the way down to the ground.

19
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:41,000
That is why Beji and his followers ended up tumbling through the wind.

20
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,420
So when that tree collapsed,

21
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,920
the entepung pillar/tree of Beji turned into stone

22
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,420
many of them became rock formations out there.

23
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:55,420
So here it is, he was almost about to reach the sky,

24
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:57,720
just a little bit more.

25
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:01,320
And so they tumbled upside down as they fell.

26
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:06,920
Sorrowful is the heart of the skilled celestial being,

27
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,870
Endo Segadok; who sent down the pattern Buah Kelekuh Ambun Belabuh

28
00:02:12,950 --> 00:02:15,870
Nyawa Rerauh Minta Tutuh Ke Raja Nyaduh.

29
00:02:15,950 --> 00:02:20,420
Buah Engeramuh, Mansau Sedan, Nurun ka Buah Kelekit Gajai Langit,

30
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,220
Nyawa Sesengit Minta Tumbit Ke Raja Tindit,

31
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:25,120
Bukit Tumpur Nyadi Emperan.

32
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:28,120
Now, this Tangga Beji pattern

33
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:31,120
was originally resist-tied (ngebat) by Dayang Kerja,

34
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:35,120
a skilled woman of former times and the wife of Sumbang Berani.

35
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:45,190
For me, my thought was, seeing what Tangga Beji

36
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:48,920
should look like without any pattern sample or model (teladan to follow),

37
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,050
I just used my own inner heart and mind -

38
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:53,020
and then went ahead and created this Tangga Beji pattern myself.

39
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:56,230
Making this Tangga Beji pattern was done without any template or pattern guide.

40
00:02:56,310 --> 00:02:59,460
It came directly from my own thoughts, straight out of my head.

41
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:03,400
This is the story of this Tangga Beji motif.

42
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:20,870
So for this piece, because this is silk thread (ubong sutera), my child,

43
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:26,110
back then, because silk thread takes directly to the engkudu [red dye].

44
00:03:26,650 --> 00:03:29,300
I insisted that I wouldn't use chemical dyes (selup);

45
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:33,320
all the pua I make, none of them use chemical dye or synthetic dye (selup / dye).

46
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:35,570
It must be engkudu [natural Morinda red dye]

47
00:03:35,650 --> 00:03:38,600
Because with this engkudu,

48
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:42,330
even if you wash it, or if it gets wet, the color will not bleed or fade.

49
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:45,000
This red one, is dyed 8 times using engkudu.

50
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:50,750
I cooked it for an hour and a half.

51
00:03:56,050 --> 00:04:05,250
For this blue/black, this is made from renggat or tarum.

52
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,620
Now, for this blue portion:

53
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:12,670
we tie it (kebat) first, and then after we untie it,

54
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:15,750
that is when it becomes blue.

55
00:04:16,570 --> 00:04:18,770
Now, for this resist-tying process (ngebat):

56
00:04:18,850 --> 00:04:21,000
originally, lemba was collected and used.

57
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:24,120
But now, because my physical strength is no longer what it used to be,

58
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:28,500
I use synthetic/plastic string instead, though you still must use wax (lilin) with it.

59
00:04:29,150 --> 00:04:31,570
We twist it -

60
00:04:31,650 --> 00:04:34,570
if we don't twist it when forming its loop (gelung),

61
00:04:34,650 --> 00:04:36,670
it won't turn out well.

62
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:42,980
This is what I do when I do this.

63
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:48,820
As for the time it took me to make this Tangga Beji back then,

64
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:52,770
right from when I started winding the warp threads (Ngirit),

65
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:55,770
it took me about a month to finish it completely.

66
00:04:55,850 --> 00:04:58,770
For this engkudu colour,

67
00:04:58,850 --> 00:05:03,390
it depends on the weather. If it is not sunny, it would not dry even for three days.

68
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:06,900
Then comes the second layer of resist-wrapping (pampul ke 2),

69
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:09,520
after which it enters this stage. Once that dries,

70
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:18,060
it is cut away (ketas). Only after all that does it end up looking like this.

71
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:22,400
You can even wash this, my child.

72
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:28,300
If you are willing, you can wash it.

73
00:05:31,550 --> 00:05:35,190
The reason I created this Tangga Beji pattern back then was

74
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:40,120
because in our longhouse community, I hadn't seen anyone make it, though I had heard the stories.

75
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:44,570
So I drew it out from my own mind, treating it as a form of sacred teaching (jaku ajar).

76
00:05:44,650 --> 00:05:49,520
The reason Beji wanted to reach the heavens was that

77
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:53,300
he was waiting for Aji to return, but he never did

78
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:56,880
because he had jumped off the edge of the sky (nyumping pintu langit).

79
00:05:56,960 --> 00:06:00,970
Beji wants to follow his brother, but then again,

80
00:06:01,050 --> 00:06:05,330
the Tiang Entepung is not sturdy.

81
00:06:05,650 --> 00:06:09,220
For me, in my opinion, I don't copy other people's work.

82
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:17,870
Nobody made the Tangga Beji Pua which originated from Sungai Kain.

83
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:20,870
So I decided to make it myself.

84
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:24,270
And so I created it entirely in my mind,

85
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:29,170
, so that it would serve as a memory - to serve as an example (contoh).

86
00:06:29,250 --> 00:06:32,420
This stands as a moral lesson (jaku ajar) for everyone:

87
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:36,200
the reason why he was so determined to reach the heavens was to follow Aji

88
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,330
their eldest brother.

89
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:41,470
Aji is not able to return from the sky.

90
00:06:41,550 --> 00:06:48,570
Therfore, Beji wants to follow him.

91
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:50,770
To take them as an example,

92
00:06:50,850 --> 00:06:55,420
like siblings - because there were only five siblings altogether

93
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:59,420
according to the elders' stories (cherita tuai).

94
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:02,420
I thought about it, I wanted to have a reference pattern,

95
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:07,870
I wanted to see someone else’s Tangga Beji motif,

96
00:07:07,950 --> 00:07:13,970
but because there wasn't one, I created it myself to serve as an example,

97
00:07:14,050 --> 00:07:18,620
to serve as a guide. So that when I am no longer around,

98
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,620
so that my children, grandchildren, and all of our people

99
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:26,670
will remember the meaning behind this Tangga Beji pattern

100
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:32,470
I would like to thank you all, because of all my Pua,

101
00:07:32,550 --> 00:07:35,550
you chose the story of Tangga Beji. Thank you.

102
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:43,720
The reason I made this Tangga Beji pattern is

103
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:47,320
because it serves as a moral teaching (jaku ajar),

104
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:52,220
to serve as a memory

105
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:56,900
for mothers and children, and for their future children and great-grandchildren.

106
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:00,580
That is its true meaning. In this way, all of us will remember the story

107
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:03,520
behind Beji's heartache and his desperate

108
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:07,260
longing to be reunited with his brother, Aji.

109
00:08:07,750 --> 00:08:13,020
So that it would be remembered - that was my thought back then

110
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:16,020
when creating the Tangga Beji pattern,

111
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:20,770
having listened to the stories of the elders from the past.

112
00:08:20,850 --> 00:08:24,370
None of us over there made the Tangga Beji

113
00:08:24,450 --> 00:08:27,570
back then, but I conceived and created it entirely in my mind.
